{
  "//": [
    "The stack registry, as data.",
    "",
    "A stack is a curated combination of capability tags and verticals",
    "that produces a coherent greenfield project: pick one with",
    "`keel new --stack=<id>` and the engine resolves everything from",
    "there. Stacks are sugar — they add no expressive power the",
    "composition layer does not already have — and nothing in one is",
    "code, which is why they live here rather than in stacks.ts. Every",
    "field is either a literal (tags, projects, the two strings) or a",
    "reference to something registered under an id: a vertical, a build",
    "system, a module layout, a sibling stack.",
    "",
    "`src/domain/core/stacks.ts` validates this file against",
    "`StackPresetsSchema` and resolves those references at load, and",
    "`tests/domain/core/stack-registry.test.ts` freezes the result. The",
    "presets keep their order here: it is the order",
    "`Object.values(STACKS)` yields, and the wizard's grid reads it.",
    "",
    "Adding a stack: append a preset whose `tags` and `verticals`",
    "describe the desired starting point. The verticals install in array",
    "order; if order matters across them (e.g. `vcs` before",
    "`walking-skeleton`, so the project is a repo before files land),",
    "reflect that here. `buildSystems` and `moduleLayouts` are the dials",
    "the stack offers, first entry the default, and a stack declaring",
    "one omits the matching `pkg.*` / `layout.*` tag from `tags` — the",
    "install handler folds the chosen option's tag in.",
    "",
    "A composite stack declares `services` instead of scaffolding in",
    "place: each service is a full stack installed into its own",
    "subdirectory (own tree, own manifest), resolving with its siblings'",
    "`projects` tags in scope as peers. A composite's own `verticals`",
    "run at the product root. Composites cannot nest."
  ],
